{"format":"local-vault-ai-portable-chunks-v1","version":1,"chunks":[{"id":"6 - Full Notes/CSS Font Size and Inheritance.md::0","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/CSS Font Size and Inheritance.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"css font size and inheritance css font size and inheritance","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/CSS Font Size and Inheritance.md","fileName":"CSS Font Size and Inheritance.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"CSS Font Size and Inheritance","heading":"Document","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"2026-09-14 01:58\n\nStatus: #baby\n\nTags: [[CSS Web Typography]]","tags":["baby"],"links":["CSS Web Typography","css_thedefinitiveguide.pdf"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""},{"id":"6 - Full Notes/CSS Font Size and Inheritance.md::1","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/CSS Font Size and Inheritance.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"css font size and inheritance css font size and inheritance","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/CSS Font Size and Inheritance.md","fileName":"CSS Font Size and Inheritance.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"CSS Font Size and Inheritance","heading":"CSS Font Size and Inheritance","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"The `font-size` property accepts absolute-size keywords, relative-size keywords, lengths, and percentages. Relative keywords and percentages are calculated from the inherited font size, while units such as `em` and `rem` refer to element or root font metrics.\n\nChildren inherit the computed font size rather than re-running the parent's original percentage expression. This prevents a percentage from compounding at every generation unless it is explicitly declared again.","tags":["baby"],"links":["CSS Web Typography","css_thedefinitiveguide.pdf"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""},{"id":"6 - Full Notes/CSS Font Size and Inheritance.md::2","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/CSS Font Size and Inher